      "urpx:hasCoverageClaim": {
        "@id": "gpc:cc-pps-2026-06-01",
        "@type": "urpx:CoverageClaim",
        "urpx:completenessResult": {
          "@id": "urpx:partial"
        },
        "urpx:selfContained": true,
        "urpx:explainedBy": {
          "@type": "urpx:Evaluation",
          "@id": "gpc:cc-pps-2026-06-01-evaluation",
          "urpx:evaluationKind": {
            "@id": "urpx:coverageEvaluation"
          },
          "urpx:description": "This filing does not carry everything its source document states. 5 parts are deferred, listed here in the same words as the filing's tariff.toml [modeling].deferrals so the two records cannot drift. (1) Fuel seasons by billing month. FCR-27 prices June through September and October through May, which Schedule R's bills show is read by the billing month a bill is rendered in. The JSON-LD gates the fuel PriceDefinitions on calendar months, as PPS-11's own energy seasons are, so usage in the weeks a billing period runs ahead of its billing month takes the other season's fuel price. No PPS bill was available to show how a pre-paid account's billing month is set. (2) Municipal Franchise Fee base. MFF-11 applies to the total revenues of each bill, which include the ECCR-15 and DSM-R-16 amounts. Its multiplier Prices here are based on the energy-and-fuel subtotal and on the Basic Service Charge Price, not on the ECCR and DSM-R multiplier Prices, so the franchise fee on those two amounts, about 0.44 percent of the base bill inside city limits, is not carried. (3) Minimum Bill. The sheet sets it at the Basic Service Charge, while service is connected and for up to ten days after disconnection, plus ECCR, DSM-R and the Municipal Franchise Fee, and no Price carries it. Every energy and fuel price here is positive, so a bill on these prices alone is never below it while service is connected; the ten days of Basic Service Charge after a disconnection are not carried. (4) Pre-payment terms and Term of Contract. The sheet requires a $40.00 minimum positive balance to connect, disconnects service when the balance reaches $0.00, requires a minimum payment covering usage up to disconnection, any reconnect fees under Rule F3 and a $5.00 minimum pre-payment to reconnect, adds any Account Establishment Charge under Rule E2 before connection, and sets a term that \"varies based on pre-paid amount and customer electric consumption\". None of these is a price per unit of service and none is carried. (5) Fuel Cost Recovery voltage levels. FCR-27 also prices Primary Distribution and Transmission customers. Only the Secondary Distribution rates are carried, as Prices with no condition, so they apply to every customer on the schedule.",
          "urpx:evaluatedOn": "2026-10-17T00:00:00"
        }
      }
    }
  }
